Add a shared Wi-Fi OTA transaction core to the Aliro door-lock
reader firmware. Applied only to nanoc6-wifi and atoms3-lite-wifi
via variants.json; nanoc6-thread never applies, compiles, links,
or exposes any of the code introduced here.

Scope, kept minimal (no HTTP route, no page UI, no UDP or TCP
server, no authentication, no restart, no settings changes, no
log-capture changes):

  * NEW main/aliro_local_ota.h: declares the four-entry-point
    transaction core (Begin / Write / Finish / Abort) that later
    Wi-Fi entry points (an HTTP handler in a later patch, and an
    espota server in a later patch) share. The header is present
    only on Wi-Fi variants.

  * NEW main/aliro_local_ota.cpp: implements the state machine:
      - A short portMUX critical section guards a single busy
        flag s_busy. Only one transaction may be active at a
        time; a concurrent second Begin returns
        ESP_ERR_INVALID_STATE and does NOT take the guard.
      - Begin selects the next OTA partition with
        esp_ota_get_next_update_partition, refuses a declared
        size that is 0 or greater than that partition, and
        calls esp_ota_begin. On any failure the busy guard is
        released before returning.
      - Write buffers the first 288 bytes (image header +
        first segment header + full app descriptor) into a
        fixed static prefix; no per-write allocation. Once the
        prefix is full it verifies the ESP image magic byte
        0xE9, the incoming chip id against the running chip
        (ESP32-C6 or ESP32-S3, gated by CONFIG_IDF_TARGET_*),
        the app descriptor magic word 0xABCD5432, and the
        incoming project_name against esp_app_get_description
        of the running app. On mismatch the transaction is
        aborted (esp_ota_abort + busy release) and the failure
        is returned. Only after successful validation is the
        buffered prefix forwarded to esp_ota_write and only
        then are subsequent bytes forwarded directly.
      - Overflow-safe write-size guard. len is untrusted, so
        s_received_size + len is NEVER evaluated. Every write
        first proves s_received_size <= s_declared_size (the
        invariant established at Begin and preserved by every
        path that increments the counter — the runtime check
        is at the top of Write), then rejects when
        len > s_declared_size - s_received_size. A SIZE_MAX-
        style len therefore aborts with ESP_ERR_INVALID_SIZE
        instead of wrapping past the guard.
      - Finish requires a validated prefix and an exact
        received-size match against the declared size; else
        the transaction is aborted. It calls esp_ota_end and
        sets the boot partition with esp_ota_set_boot_partition
        ONLY on esp_ota_end success (complete image
        validation). The busy guard is released before Finish
        returns in either the success or the failure path.
      - Abort is idempotent, safe from any partial-write or
        error path and from a state where no transaction is
        open, and never blocks on Wi-Fi or Matter.

  * WIRE the new patch into nanoc6-wifi and atoms3-lite-wifi
    source_patches in firmware/variants.json.
    nanoc6-thread source_patches is unchanged.

Explicit non-goals for this patch: no HTTP route, no page UI, no
UDP or TCP server, no authentication, no compiled-in Wi-Fi
credentials, no cJSON or new runtime dependency, no external
asset, no partition change, no restart, no settings or log
changes, no build-system changes (the main/ SRC_DIRS glob picks
up the new .cpp automatically on Wi-Fi variants).

diff --git a/examples/door_lock/main/aliro_local_ota.h b/examples/door_lock/main/aliro_local_ota.h
new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/examples/door_lock/main/aliro_local_ota.h
@@ -0,0 +1,89 @@
+/*
+   Shared Wi-Fi OTA transaction core for the Aliro door-lock reader
+   firmware. Compiled and linked only on the Wi-Fi variants
+   (nanoc6-wifi and atoms3-lite-wifi). The Thread variant never
+   applies, compiles, or links this module.
+
+   The module is a single-transfer OTA state machine that later
+   Wi-Fi entry points (an HTTP handler in a later patch, and an
+   espota server in a later patch) share. It does not open any
+   HTTP route, page, UDP or TCP socket by itself, and it does not
+   restart the device. On complete success it sets the boot
+   partition and returns; the caller decides when to reboot.
+
+   Concurrency: only one transaction may be active at a time. A
+   short portMUX critical section guards a single busy flag. The
+   caller must serialise writes on a single transaction.
+*/
+
+#pragma once
+
+#include <esp_err.h>
+#include <stddef.h>
+
+#ifdef __cplusplus
+extern "C" {
+#endif
+
+/*
+   Open a single-transfer OTA transaction with the declared
+   image size in bytes.
+
+   On success takes the shared busy guard, selects the next OTA
+   partition with esp_ota_get_next_update_partition, refuses the
+   declared size if it is 0 or greater than the selected
+   partition, and calls esp_ota_begin.
+
+   On any failure this function releases the busy guard before
+   returning. A concurrent second call while a transaction is
+   already open returns ESP_ERR_INVALID_STATE and does NOT take
+   the busy guard.
+*/
+esp_err_t AliroLocalOtaBegin(size_t declared_size);
+
+/*
+   Append at most len bytes to the active transaction.
+
+   Requires an open transaction; else ESP_ERR_INVALID_STATE and
+   NO state change. If the running total plus len would exceed
+   the declared size, the transaction is aborted and
+   ESP_ERR_INVALID_SIZE is returned.
+
+   The first bytes are buffered into a small fixed prefix. Once
+   the prefix is full, the early ESP image header chip id and
+   the app descriptor magic word and project name are compared
+   against the running app. On mismatch the transaction is
+   aborted (esp_ota_abort + release of the busy guard) and the
+   failure is returned. Only after successful validation is the
+   buffered prefix forwarded to esp_ota_write, and only then
+   are the subsequent bytes forwarded directly.
+
+   No per-write allocation. The prefix buffer is a fixed static.
+*/
+esp_err_t AliroLocalOtaWrite(const void *data, size_t len);
+
+/*
+   Complete the transaction.
+
+   Requires an open transaction with a validated prefix and an
+   exact received-size match against the declared size; else the
+   transaction is aborted and ESP_ERR_INVALID_STATE or
+   ESP_ERR_INVALID_SIZE is returned.
+
+   On success calls esp_ota_end and, ONLY on esp_ota_end success
+   (complete image validation), calls esp_ota_set_boot_partition.
+   In either the success or failure path the busy guard is
+   released before this function returns.
+*/
+esp_err_t AliroLocalOtaFinish(void);
+
+/*
+   Abort the active transaction and release the busy guard.
+   Idempotent; safe to call from any partial-write or error
+   path, and from a state where no transaction is open.
+*/
+void AliroLocalOtaAbort(void);
+
+#ifdef __cplusplus
+}
+#endif
diff --git a/examples/door_lock/main/aliro_local_ota.cpp b/examples/door_lock/main/aliro_local_ota.cpp
new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/examples/door_lock/main/aliro_local_ota.cpp
@@ -0,0 +1,299 @@
+/*
+   Shared Wi-Fi OTA transaction core for the Aliro door-lock reader
+   firmware. Wi-Fi variants only (nanoc6-wifi, atoms3-lite-wifi);
+   the Thread variant never applies, compiles, or links this file.
+
+   Non-goals in this module: no HTTP route, no page UI, no UDP or TCP
+   server, no authentication, no restart, no settings or log
+   changes. This is a bare state machine that later Wi-Fi entry
+   points share.
+
+   State ownership:
+
+     * A short portMUX critical section guards a single busy flag
+       s_busy.
+     * All other state (s_handle, s_partition, s_declared_size,
+       s_received_size, s_prefix, s_prefix_len, s_prefix_validated)
+       is single-writer while s_busy is true and the caller has the
+       transaction open. The caller must serialise writes on a
+       single transaction.
+*/
+
+#include "aliro_local_ota.h"
+
+#include <string.h>
+
+#include <esp_app_desc.h>
+#include <esp_app_format.h>
+#include <esp_log.h>
+#include <esp_ota_ops.h>
+#include <esp_partition.h>
+#include <freertos/FreeRTOS.h>
+#include <freertos/portmacro.h>
+
+namespace {
+
+const char *TAG = "aliro_ota";
+
+/*
+   The prefix buffer must hold at least the ESP image header
+   (24 bytes), the first segment header (8 bytes), and the app
+   descriptor (256 bytes). That is 288 bytes total. The buffer
+   is a fixed static; nothing here calls malloc.
+*/
+constexpr size_t kAliroOtaPrefixBytes =
+    sizeof(esp_image_header_t) + sizeof(esp_image_segment_header_t) +
+    sizeof(esp_app_desc_t);
+static_assert(kAliroOtaPrefixBytes == 288,
+              "prefix buffer must be exactly image header + segment "
+              "header + app descriptor");
+
+portMUX_TYPE s_ota_lock = portMUX_INITIALIZER_UNLOCKED;
+bool s_busy = false;
+
+esp_ota_handle_t s_handle = 0;
+const esp_partition_t *s_partition = nullptr;
+size_t s_declared_size = 0;
+size_t s_received_size = 0;
+uint8_t s_prefix[kAliroOtaPrefixBytes] = {0};
+size_t s_prefix_len = 0;
+bool s_prefix_validated = false;
+
+/*
+   Try to take the shared busy guard. Returns true if this call
+   observed s_busy == false and set it to true; false if a
+   transaction was already open.
+*/
+bool try_take_busy() {
+    portENTER_CRITICAL(&s_ota_lock);
+    bool was_busy = s_busy;
+    if (!was_busy) {
+        s_busy = true;
+    }
+    portEXIT_CRITICAL(&s_ota_lock);
+    return !was_busy;
+}
+
+/*
+   Release the shared busy guard. The caller must have taken it
+   via try_take_busy earlier. Idempotent from the outside because
+   the abort path checks s_busy before doing anything.
+*/
+void release_busy() {
+    portENTER_CRITICAL(&s_ota_lock);
+    s_busy = false;
+    portEXIT_CRITICAL(&s_ota_lock);
+}
+
+/*
+   Reset all per-transaction state. Only call this while s_busy
+   is true and the caller owns the transaction.
+*/
+void reset_state() {
+    s_handle = 0;
+    s_partition = nullptr;
+    s_declared_size = 0;
+    s_received_size = 0;
+    s_prefix_len = 0;
+    s_prefix_validated = false;
+    memset(s_prefix, 0, sizeof(s_prefix));
+}
+
+/*
+   Compare the buffered prefix against the running app. Returns
+   ESP_OK if the incoming image is compatible; ESP_ERR_INVALID_ARG
+   on any mismatch. Does NOT modify state and does NOT touch the
+   OTA handle.
+*/
+esp_err_t validate_prefix() {
+    if (s_prefix_len < kAliroOtaPrefixBytes) {
+        return ESP_ERR_INVALID_STATE;
+    }
+    const esp_image_header_t *hdr =
+        reinterpret_cast<const esp_image_header_t *>(s_prefix);
+    if (hdr->magic != ESP_IMAGE_HEADER_MAGIC) {
+        ESP_LOGE(TAG, "image magic 0x%02x != 0xE9",
+                 static_cast<unsigned>(hdr->magic));
+        return ESP_ERR_INVALID_ARG;
+    }
+    const esp_app_desc_t *incoming =
+        reinterpret_cast<const esp_app_desc_t *>(
+            s_prefix + sizeof(esp_image_header_t) +
+            sizeof(esp_image_segment_header_t));
+    if (incoming->magic_word != ESP_APP_DESC_MAGIC_WORD) {
+        ESP_LOGE(TAG, "app desc magic 0x%08x != 0xABCD5432",
+                 static_cast<unsigned>(incoming->magic_word));
+        return ESP_ERR_INVALID_ARG;
+    }
+#if defined(CONFIG_IDF_TARGET_ESP32C6)
+    if (hdr->chip_id != ESP_CHIP_ID_ESP32C6) {
+        ESP_LOGE(TAG, "image chip id 0x%04x != running ESP32-C6",
+                 static_cast<unsigned>(hdr->chip_id));
+        return ESP_ERR_INVALID_ARG;
+    }
+#elif defined(CONFIG_IDF_TARGET_ESP32S3)
+    if (hdr->chip_id != ESP_CHIP_ID_ESP32S3) {
+        ESP_LOGE(TAG, "image chip id 0x%04x != running ESP32-S3",
+                 static_cast<unsigned>(hdr->chip_id));
+        return ESP_ERR_INVALID_ARG;
+    }
+#else
+#error "aliro_local_ota: unsupported target chip"
+#endif
+    const esp_app_desc_t *running = esp_app_get_description();
+    if (running == nullptr) {
+        return ESP_ERR_INVALID_STATE;
+    }
+    if (strncmp(incoming->project_name, running->project_name,
+                sizeof(incoming->project_name)) != 0) {
+        ESP_LOGE(TAG, "project name mismatch");
+        return ESP_ERR_INVALID_ARG;
+    }
+    return ESP_OK;
+}
+
+}  // namespace
+
+esp_err_t AliroLocalOtaBegin(size_t declared_size) {
+    if (declared_size == 0) {
+        return ESP_ERR_INVALID_ARG;
+    }
+    if (!try_take_busy()) {
+        return ESP_ERR_INVALID_STATE;
+    }
+    reset_state();
+    s_partition = esp_ota_get_next_update_partition(nullptr);
+    if (s_partition == nullptr) {
+        release_busy();
+        return ESP_ERR_NOT_FOUND;
+    }
+    if (declared_size > s_partition->size) {
+        release_busy();
+        return ESP_ERR_INVALID_SIZE;
+    }
+    esp_err_t err = esp_ota_begin(s_partition, declared_size, &s_handle);
+    if (err != ESP_OK) {
+        s_partition = nullptr;
+        release_busy();
+        return err;
+    }
+    s_declared_size = declared_size;
+    return ESP_OK;
+}
+
+esp_err_t AliroLocalOtaWrite(const void *data, size_t len) {
+    if (data == nullptr && len > 0) {
+        return ESP_ERR_INVALID_ARG;
+    }
+    portENTER_CRITICAL(&s_ota_lock);
+    bool active = s_busy && s_handle != 0;
+    portEXIT_CRITICAL(&s_ota_lock);
+    if (!active) {
+        return ESP_ERR_INVALID_STATE;
+    }
+    if (len == 0) {
+        return ESP_OK;
+    }
+    /*
+       Overflow-safe write-size guard. len is untrusted (it comes
+       from a caller that ultimately reads it off the network) and
+       may be as large as SIZE_MAX, so s_received_size + len must
+       never be evaluated. The invariant s_received_size <=
+       s_declared_size is checked below and preserved by every
+       path that increments s_received_size, so
+       s_declared_size - s_received_size is always a valid
+       subtraction; comparing len against it detects overflow
+       without wrap.
+    */
+    if (s_received_size > s_declared_size) {
+        AliroLocalOtaAbort();
+        return ESP_ERR_INVALID_STATE;
+    }
+    if (len > s_declared_size - s_received_size) {
+        AliroLocalOtaAbort();
+        return ESP_ERR_INVALID_SIZE;
+    }
+    const uint8_t *p = static_cast<const uint8_t *>(data);
+    if (!s_prefix_validated) {
+        size_t want = kAliroOtaPrefixBytes - s_prefix_len;
+        size_t take = (len < want) ? len : want;
+        memcpy(s_prefix + s_prefix_len, p, take);
+        s_prefix_len += take;
+        if (s_prefix_len < kAliroOtaPrefixBytes) {
+            s_received_size += take;
+            return ESP_OK;
+        }
+        esp_err_t v = validate_prefix();
+        if (v != ESP_OK) {
+            AliroLocalOtaAbort();
+            return v;
+        }
+        s_prefix_validated = true;
+        esp_err_t w = esp_ota_write(s_handle, s_prefix,
+                                    kAliroOtaPrefixBytes);
+        if (w != ESP_OK) {
+            AliroLocalOtaAbort();
+            return w;
+        }
+        s_received_size += take;
+        p += take;
+        len -= take;
+        if (len == 0) {
+            return ESP_OK;
+        }
+    }
+    esp_err_t w = esp_ota_write(s_handle, p, len);
+    if (w != ESP_OK) {
+        AliroLocalOtaAbort();
+        return w;
+    }
+    s_received_size += len;
+    return ESP_OK;
+}
+
+esp_err_t AliroLocalOtaFinish(void) {
+    portENTER_CRITICAL(&s_ota_lock);
+    bool active = s_busy && s_handle != 0;
+    portEXIT_CRITICAL(&s_ota_lock);
+    if (!active) {
+        return ESP_ERR_INVALID_STATE;
+    }
+    if (!s_prefix_validated) {
+        AliroLocalOtaAbort();
+        return ESP_ERR_INVALID_STATE;
+    }
+    if (s_received_size != s_declared_size) {
+        AliroLocalOtaAbort();
+        return ESP_ERR_INVALID_SIZE;
+    }
+    esp_ota_handle_t handle = s_handle;
+    const esp_partition_t *partition = s_partition;
+    esp_err_t end_err = esp_ota_end(handle);
+    if (end_err != ESP_OK) {
+        s_handle = 0;
+        s_partition = nullptr;
+        release_busy();
+        return end_err;
+    }
+    esp_err_t boot_err = esp_ota_set_boot_partition(partition);
+    s_handle = 0;
+    s_partition = nullptr;
+    release_busy();
+    return boot_err;
+}
+
+void AliroLocalOtaAbort(void) {
+    portENTER_CRITICAL(&s_ota_lock);
+    if (!s_busy) {
+        portEXIT_CRITICAL(&s_ota_lock);
+        return;
+    }
+    esp_ota_handle_t handle = s_handle;
+    s_handle = 0;
+    s_partition = nullptr;
+    portEXIT_CRITICAL(&s_ota_lock);
+    if (handle != 0) {
+        esp_ota_abort(handle);
+    }
+    release_busy();
+}
